# the second of the two answers `AST::OwnershipPass::ensure_deinit` can give, and the one that keeps the
# hot path from growing a frame: `Handle`'s fields are a pointer and a `usize`, so its teardown never has to
# reach inside the value and there is nothing for a synthesized body to hold
--- OUT --->
16
released
balanced
--- RAST --->
# the drop is the destructor the author wrote, called directly
CHECK: call destructor(addrof<Handle&>(varref<Handle>(var($h))))
--- IR --->
CHECK: define i32 @main(

# and no body was synthesized for it. `$deinit` appears in this program for the types that do need one -
# `string`, `array` - but never for `Handle`, whose mangled owner segment would put its name in the symbol
CHECK-NOT: Handle_$deinit
